AD  - King Mongkut's University of Technology, Faculty of Technical Education, Department of Teacher Training in Electrical Engineering, North Bangkok, Thailand
AB  - The paper aims to present the development of a competence-based curriculum for off-grid solar installation using IoT technology to enhance the installation and operation skill as well as the application of IoT technology for energy monitoring. The research data is collected from a training course in four-years student with a target group of 30 undergraduate students of electrical engineering and education program in electrical power major. The research findings indicate that the tasks, abilities, behavioral objectives, skills, content, exercises, and assessments of the curriculum align cohesively. The evaluation of the curriculum of suitability in terms of details, usability, and content relevance indicates the highest level of suitability. Additionally, the satisfaction assessment results of course users were at a highest level. The assessment of the developed curriculum's effectiveness meets the criteria of E1/E2, achieving an efficiency score of 86.41/86.89 respectively, demonstrating its high performance.  © 2023 IEEE.
