AB  - Competency Based Learning is an emerging curriculum in Kenya that provides students with a well-rounded education focused on learning both foundational and practical skills. The Competency Based Curriculum (CBC) was recently introduced but is not integrating well into the current system because there is a lack of instructor training and knowledge in the new educational program. The CBC incorporates digital literacy; however, it does not provide schools with the necessary technology. Through two experiments performed in Kisumu, Kenya, the time saved using a tablet as an assessment tool and time to learn an unfamiliar educational app were quantified. Instructor comfort level was also recorded. It was found that instructors were able to comfortably use multiple tablets to assess multiple students at the same time. Additionally, a tutorial video was sufficient for them learn to assess a student and perform basic tasks.  © 2023 IEEE.
