AB  - In this paper we present a data-driven Competency Based Training and Assessment (CBTA)-assistance system for estimation of competency grades during simulator training of pilots. Its core module is a behavioral analysis framework, that estimates performance metrics from observations of pilot trainee behavior in an XR training simulation environment. For the realization of CBTA, dependable quantifiable and context-aware information of the trainee's behavior is essential. We extract information of flight state and pilot-machine interaction from the simulator software, we model the 3-D scene of the cockpit environment and incorporate the trainee's gaze information from the eye tracking technology and the head pose using 3-D tracking from a Varjo XR3 headset, which is part of the flight simulator. With this information we achieve a deep temporal and spatial understanding of interaction, behavior and visual attention of the pilot. Our behavioral analysis framework models the pilot's behavior from observations using somatic indicators and sensors and deducts competency skill levels of the pilot, following the CBTA guidelines of the European Union Aviation Safety Agency (EASA). With our work we contribute an assistive system for pilots and flight training instructors, aiming to complement and improve assessment of training performance, providing additional information.  © 2025 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
