AB  - The application of mastery learning, where students progress through their learning in a self-paced manner until they have mastered specific concepts, is considered appealing for teaching introductory programming courses. Despite its growing popularity in computing and its extensive use in other disciplines, there is no overview of the design of courses that use mastery learning. In this position paper, we present an overview of five mastery learning models and discuss examples of how these can be applied in practice, both in foundational programming as well as more advanced courses. Our analysis focuses on the student progression through the course, the assessment structure, and the support for self-paced learning, including for struggling students. This work provides a greater understanding of mastery learning and its application in a computing education context. © 2025 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
