AB  - In the context of energy transition, sustainable development, and deep international integration, integrating energy technical standards into engineering education is essential for Vietnam. This paper examines the role of energy standards in developing a qualified technical workforce, particularly in electricity, renewable energy, and environmental engineering. By synthesizing international experiences from the European Union, Japan, and South Korea, it highlights effective curriculum models and evaluates current policies and practices in Vietnam's technical education. The study identifies major challenges, including the absence of standardized frameworks, limited faculty capacity, weak university-industry-standards linkages, and a lack of competency-based assessment systems. It concludes by proposing key policy and institutional solutions to enhance standard integration in education, contributing to workforce standardization and national competitiveness.  © 2025 IEEE.
