AB  - Assessment is a very relevant part of any instructional process. Its results, when adequately provided, can improve students’ learning. Assessment results could also be used to guide teachers in order to align their course design with the students’ results. However, the analysis of the assessment results and the extraction of useful conclusions for both teachers and students is not an easy task and computerized tools can be very helpful to provide automation of these processes. Moreover, the information regarding assessment of students can come from many sources and in the case of blended learning environments, the number of sources increases. In this paper, a system aimed at supporting Competence-based Learning in blended learning environments (COBLE) is presented. The paper presents the system’s architecture and its main elements. It is specially described how information from different sources can be gathered together into the s stem in order to u date its models and anal ze the assessment data as a whole Copyright © 2018 for this paper by its authors.
