AB  - This study explores IT curriculum reform in vocational-technical education (VTE) using the Photoshop CS6 (PS CS6) course as a case study. We integrate the Analytic Hierarchy Process (AHP) to align educational outcomes with modern workforce demands, emphasizing competency-based learning and industry relevance. Our approach restructures curricula, implements modern assessment techniques, and leverages the 'Tian Jiabing Cup' competition to bridge academia-industry gaps. Results show a 98% student learning efficiency and significant skill enhancement, validating the model's efficacy in preparing graduates for evolving technological landscapes. © 2025 IEEE.
