AB  - Competency-based education is already adopted by higher education institutions around the world. This study presents the results of an investigation carried out with engineering students. The objective is focused on exploring aspects of innovations in teaching and learning through a competence assessment procedure and some aspects of gamification. The goal is to improve content learning, as well as the academic performance of the students. Cycloid is the ICT tool used in previous years for the assessment of competencies. The study showed some results detected as weaknesses by the student. As a prevention measure, it was decided to introduce gamification as the strategy in the subject of technical drawing in the Degree in Engineering in Industrial Technologies at the University of Girona. This contribution describes a practical experience through the use of certain aspects of gamification during the course 2019–2020, student’s motivation, and acquisition of competencies. We worked with a total of 78 students. In conclusion, comparing with previous studies, the academic results obtained were positive and the students were more enthusiastic about this subject. They also collaborated to continue team working, creating a good atmosphere. They also faced the change in weaknesses observed in the assessment of competencies, positively. © 2022, The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG.
