AB  - As advanced technologies become increasingly integrated across all fields, it is necessary to make interventions in both academic and industrial domains. Industries seek out college graduates with strong academic credentials, digital literacy, technological proficiency, and essential soft skills like critical thinking, problem-solving, teamwork, and management. Traditionally, student performance has been evaluated based on an overall GPA score. However, this cumulative score fails to provide a detailed reflection of students' competence at the level of the course Learning Objectives (LOs). Consequently, it becomes challenging to identify specific strengths and weaknesses in technical areas. The constructive alignment framework offers an outcome-driven approach in which it defines a set of LOs for each course in the program and aligns teaching and assessment methods around it to fulfill those objectives. This framework has garnered recent attention in higher education due to the expansion of subjects and the diverse skills required for the 5th industrial revolution. In this study, we propose an AI-assisted system that adopts this framework and identifies students' learning gaps at the level of course LOs, and recommends courses to fill these knowledge gaps and also meet the expectations of prospective job positions. This comprehensive approach helps students acquire the technical knowledge necessary to align with their career goals.  © 2023 Owner/Author.
