AB  - In the modern system of higher education, the use of an electronic portfolio (e-portfolio) is becoming increasingly relevant. The e-portfolio acts as tool that allows you to accumulate and present evidence of the development of these competencies in a structured manner, which is in line with the concept of a competency-based approach in education and the requirements of stakeholders for the quality of personnel training. Research in the field of pedagogy and education management confirms the need to develop and implement systems for assessing and demonstrating competencies that go beyond traditional academic assessments. The introduction of IT in the educational process has become a necessity, and the eportfolio acts as an effective means of integrating these technologies into the educational process. The purpose of our study was to test the hypothesis that the level of motivation of students who have access to comparing their achievements with the achievements of the group will be higher than that of students who do not use the e-portfolio. The subject of the study is the use of e-portfolio in the educational process of engineering universities. The task of the study is to experimentally check and compare the indicators of student groups in educational, research, sports and social public blocks. The work used such methods as analysis of the research problem, scientific and methodological literature, analysis of the principles of formation of the e-portfolio created by the staff of engineering universities. As a result of the pedagogical experiment, conclusions were made about the effectiveness of using the e-portfolio in the classroom and independent work of students  © 2025 IEEE.
