AB  - This paper presents a human-centric, co-designed e-learning framework that leverages artificial intelligence (AI) to address skill gaps in primary education. Aligned with Thailand's national education reforms and the Rayong MARCO competency model, the framework supports competency-based assessment in Thai, English, and Mathematics. Developed on the Moodle platform, the system integrates AI-driven features such as automated exam checking, image and voice recognition for skill assessment, and performance analytics to enhance evaluation accuracy and reduce teacher workload. The development followed a participatory, agile process involving students, teachers, and education officials to ensure the system's relevance and usability in real-world classrooms. Pilot testing with Grade 3 and Grade 6 students in Rayong Province demonstrated the framework's effectiveness in identifying student competencies and addressing individual learning needs. The results suggest that combining AI technologies with human-centered design can significantly improve educational equity and help close skill gaps in diverse learning environments.  © 2025 IEEE.
